---
import LearnArticle from "../../components/LearnArticle.astro";
import DemoFrame from "../../components/DemoFrame.astro";
import RelatedLink from "../../components/RelatedLink.astro";

const BANDWIDTH_STEPS = [1, 2, 5, 10, 25, 50, 100, 250, 500, 1000];
const LATENCY_STEPS = [5, 10, 20, 40, 80, 150, 300, 600, 800];
const presets = [
	{ label: "Home fiber", bw: 500, lat: 10 },
	{ label: "Phone data", bw: 25, lat: 50 },
	{ label: "Busy café Wi-Fi", bw: 2, lat: 80 },
	{ label: "Satellite", bw: 50, lat: 600 },
];
---

<LearnArticle
	href="/learn/bandwidth-and-latency"
	description="Bandwidth vs latency, felt rather than just read: drag the sliders to see why a fast connection can still feel slow, with a live video-buffering demo."
	lead="Your internet plan says it's fast. So why does a video call still lag? Because 'fast' means two different things."
>
	<section class="block">
		<p class="block-title">A Highway, Two Ways</p>
		<p class="block-text">
			Picture data as cars driving along a highway from a website to you.
		</p>
		<div class="compare-grid">
			<div class="compare-card compare-card--accent">
				<p class="compare-card-title">Bandwidth = how many lanes</p>
				<p>More lanes let more cars through at once. High bandwidth means lots of data can arrive every second.</p>
				<p>It's the most data that can be sent in a given amount of time — measured in bits per second, usually <em>megabits per second</em> (Mbps).</p>
			</div>
			<div class="compare-card">
				<p class="compare-card-title">Latency = how long the drive takes</p>
				<p>Even on an empty highway, the first car takes time to arrive. Latency is that delay before anything shows up.</p>
				<p>Measured in <em>milliseconds</em> (ms) — thousandths of a second.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
		<p class="block-callout">
			Adding lanes doesn't make the drive any shorter. Bandwidth and latency are separate — and different
			tasks care about different ones.
		</p>
	</section>

	<DemoFrame label="Bandwidth and latency demo">
		<div class="bl-demo" data-bl-demo data-bw-steps={JSON.stringify(BANDWIDTH_STEPS)} data-lat-steps={JSON.stringify(LATENCY_STEPS)}>
			<div class="bl-presets demo-controls">
				{presets.map((p) => <button type="button" class="demo-btn" data-bl-preset data-bw={p.bw} data-lat={p.lat}>{p.label}</button>)}
			</div>

			<div class="bl-sliders">
				<div class="bl-slider">
					<label for="bl-bw">Bandwidth</label>
					<input id="bl-bw" class="demo-range" type="range" min="0" max={BANDWIDTH_STEPS.length - 1} value="6" data-bl-bw />
					<output for="bl-bw" class="bl-slider-value" data-bl-bw-value></output>
				</div>
				<div class="bl-slider">
					<label for="bl-lat">Latency (round trip)</label>
					<input id="bl-lat" class="demo-range" type="range" min="0" max={LATENCY_STEPS.length - 1} value="3" data-bl-lat />
					<output for="bl-lat" class="bl-slider-value" data-bl-lat-value></output>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="bl-panels">
				<section class="bl-panel" aria-labelledby="bl-ping-title">
					<p class="bl-panel-title" id="bl-ping-title">Feel the latency</p>
					<div class="bl-ping-track" aria-hidden="true">
						<span class="bl-ping-end">You</span>
						<span class="bl-ping-line"><span class="bl-ping-dot" data-bl-dot></span></span>
						<span class="bl-ping-end">Server</span>
					</div>
					<div class="demo-controls">
						<button type="button" class="demo-btn demo-btn--primary" data-bl-ping>Send a message</button>
					</div>
					<p class="bl-panel-result" data-bl-ping-result aria-live="polite">Tap to send — watch how long the reply takes.</p>
				</section>

				<section class="bl-panel" aria-labelledby="bl-video-title">
					<p class="bl-panel-title" id="bl-video-title">Feel the bandwidth</p>
					<div class="demo-field bl-quality">
						<label for="bl-quality">Video quality</label>
						<select id="bl-quality" class="demo-select" data-bl-quality>
							<option value="1.5">Standard (1.5 Mbps)</option>
							<option value="5" selected>HD (5 Mbps)</option>
							<option value="25">4K (25 Mbps)</option>
						</select>
					</div>
					<div class="bl-video" aria-hidden="true">
						<div class="bl-video-screen" data-bl-screen>▶</div>
						<div class="bl-video-bar">
							<span class="bl-video-buffered" data-bl-buffered></span>
							<span class="bl-video-played" data-bl-played></span>
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="demo-controls">
						<button type="button" class="demo-btn demo-btn--primary" data-bl-play>Play video</button>
					</div>
					<p class="bl-panel-result" data-bl-video-result aria-live="polite">A 20-second clip. The light bar is what's downloaded so far.</p>
				</section>
			</div>

			<p class="bl-tasks-title">How long everyday tasks take on this connection</p>
			<ul class="bl-tasks" data-bl-tasks></ul>
			<div class="bl-legend" aria-hidden="true">
				<span><span class="bl-key bl-key--wait"></span>Waiting (latency)</span>
				<span><span class="bl-key bl-key--load"></span>Downloading (bandwidth)</span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</DemoFrame>

	<section class="block">
		<p class="block-title">Which One Matters When?</p>
		<ul class="block-list">
			<li>
				<em>Big downloads and streaming</em> — a movie, a game update, 4K video — are about{" "}
				<em>bandwidth</em>. The initial delay barely matters next to minutes of downloading.
			</li>
			<li>
				<em>Back-and-forth tasks</em> — video calls, online games, clicking around a website — are about{" "}
				<em>latency</em>. Each action has to reach the server and come back, and more lanes can't make
				that trip shorter.
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p class="block-text">
			That's why a satellite connection can stream a film perfectly well but feel sluggish in an online
			game: plenty of lanes, but a very long drive to space and back.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="block">
		<p class="block-title">Where Latency Comes From</p>
		<p class="block-text">
			Data travels through cables at close to the speed of light — incredibly fast, but not instant.
			Crossing an ocean and back takes a noticeable fraction of a second. Every router that passes your
			packets along adds a little more delay, and a busy network adds more as packets wait their turn.
		</p>
		<p class="block-text">
			That's why "just get faster internet" doesn't always fix lag: a bigger plan usually buys more
			bandwidth, while latency depends mostly on distance and how many stops your data makes along the
			way.
		</p>
		<RelatedLink href="/learn/packets-and-routing" label="How data travels" />
	</section>
</LearnArticle>

<script>
	const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-bl-demo]")!;
	const BW_STEPS: number[] = JSON.parse(root.dataset.bwSteps!);
	const LAT_STEPS: number[] = JSON.parse(root.dataset.latSteps!);

	const bwInput = root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("[data-bl-bw]")!;
	const latInput = root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("[data-bl-lat]")!;
	const bwValue = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-bl-bw-value]")!;
	const latValue = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-bl-lat-value]")!;
	const tasksEl = root.querySelector<HTMLUListElement>("[data-bl-tasks]")!;
	const dot = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-bl-dot]")!;
	const pingBtn = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-bl-ping]")!;
	const pingResult = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-bl-ping-result]")!;
	const qualitySelect = root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>("[data-bl-quality]")!;
	const screen = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-bl-screen]")!;
	const bufferedEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-bl-buffered]")!;
	const playedEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-bl-played]")!;
	const playBtn = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-bl-play]")!;
	const videoResult = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-bl-video-result]")!;

	const bandwidth = () => BW_STEPS[Number(bwInput.value)]; // Mbps
	const latency = () => LAT_STEPS[Number(latInput.value)]; // ms, round trip

	function formatSeconds(s: number): string {
		if (s < 1) return `${Math.round(s * 1000)} ms`;
		if (s < 60) return `${s < 10 ? s.toFixed(1) : Math.round(s)} seconds`;
		if (s < 3600) return `${Math.round(s / 60)} minutes`;
		const h = s / 3600;
		return `${h < 10 ? h.toFixed(1) : Math.round(h)} hours`;
	}

	// Each task: how many round trips it needs before/while loading, and how
	// many megabits it has to download.
	const TASKS = [
		{ name: "Send a chat message", trips: 1, megabits: 0.01 },
		{ name: "Load a web page (2 MB)", trips: 4, megabits: 16 },
		{ name: "Download a movie (2 GB)", trips: 1, megabits: 16000 },
	];

	function renderTasks() {
		const bw = bandwidth();
		const lat = latency() / 1000;
		tasksEl.innerHTML = "";
		TASKS.forEach((task) => {
			const wait = task.trips * lat;
			const load = task.megabits / bw;
			const total = wait + load;
			const waitPct = (wait / total) * 100;
			const li = document.createElement("li");
			li.className = "bl-task";
			li.innerHTML = `
				<span class="bl-task-name"></span>
				<span class="bl-task-bar" aria-hidden="true">
					<span class="bl-task-wait" style="width:${waitPct}%"></span><span class="bl-task-load" style="width:${100 - waitPct}%"></span>
				</span>
				<span class="bl-task-time"></span>
				<span class="bl-task-note"></span>`;
			li.querySelector(".bl-task-name")!.textContent = task.name;
			li.querySelector(".bl-task-time")!.textContent = formatSeconds(total);
			li.querySelector(".bl-task-note")!.textContent =
				waitPct > 60 ? "Mostly waiting — latency matters most" : waitPct < 40 ? "Mostly downloading — bandwidth matters most" : "A mix of both";
			tasksEl.append(li);
		});
	}

	function renderSliders() {
		bwValue.textContent = `${bandwidth()} Mbps`;
		latValue.textContent = `${latency()} ms`;
		renderTasks();
	}

	// --- Ping: the dot really takes the round-trip time to go out and back.
	let pingStart = 0;
	let pingFrame = 0;
	pingBtn.addEventListener("click", () => {
		cancelAnimationFrame(pingFrame);
		const rtt = latency();
		pingStart = performance.now();
		pingResult.textContent = "Sending…";
		const tick = (now: number) => {
			const t = Math.min(1, (now - pingStart) / rtt);
			const pos = t < 0.5 ? t * 2 : 2 - t * 2; // out, then back
			dot.style.left = `${pos * 100}%`;
			dot.classList.toggle("is-returning", t >= 0.5);
			if (t < 1) pingFrame = requestAnimationFrame(tick);
			else {
				pingResult.textContent = `Reply arrived after ${rtt} ms${rtt >= 300 ? " — you can feel that delay." : rtt <= 20 ? " — practically instant." : "."}`;
			}
		};
		pingFrame = requestAnimationFrame(tick);
	});

	// --- Video: downloads at the bandwidth, plays at normal speed, and
	// pauses to buffer whenever playback catches up with the download.
	const CLIP = 20; // seconds of video
	const START_BUFFER = 2; // seconds needed before playback starts/resumes
	let videoFrame = 0;
	let running = false;
	let last = 0;
	let startDelay = 0;
	let buffered = 0;
	let played = 0;
	let buffering = true;
	let stalls = 0;
	let waited = 0;

	function renderVideo() {
		bufferedEl.style.width = `${(buffered / CLIP) * 100}%`;
		playedEl.style.width = `${(played / CLIP) * 100}%`;
		screen.textContent = !running && played === 0 ? "▶" : buffering && played < CLIP ? "Buffering…" : played >= CLIP ? "✓" : "";
		screen.classList.toggle("is-playing", running && !buffering);
	}

	function videoTick(now: number) {
		const dt = Math.min(0.1, (now - last) / 1000);
		last = now;
		if (startDelay > 0) {
			startDelay -= dt;
			waited += dt;
		} else {
			const rate = bandwidth() / Number(qualitySelect.value); // seconds of video per second
			buffered = Math.min(CLIP, buffered + rate * dt);
		}
		if (buffering) {
			if (startDelay <= 0) waited += dt; // (the start delay was already counted above)
			if (buffered - played >= START_BUFFER || buffered >= CLIP) buffering = false;
		} else {
			played = Math.min(buffered, played + dt);
			if (played >= CLIP) {
				running = false;
				renderVideo();
				const verdict =
					stalls === 0 ? "Smooth all the way through." : `It stopped to buffer ${stalls} time${stalls === 1 ? "" : "s"}.`;
				videoResult.textContent = `${verdict} Time spent waiting: ${waited.toFixed(1)} seconds.`;
				playBtn.textContent = "Play again";
				return;
			}
			if (buffered < CLIP && buffered - played < 0.05) {
				buffering = true;
				stalls += 1;
				videoResult.textContent = "Buffering — the video caught up with the download.";
			}
		}
		renderVideo();
		videoFrame = requestAnimationFrame(videoTick);
	}

	playBtn.addEventListener("click", () => {
		cancelAnimationFrame(videoFrame);
		running = true;
		startDelay = latency() / 1000; // the request itself takes a round trip
		buffered = 0;
		played = 0;
		buffering = true;
		stalls = 0;
		waited = 0;
		playBtn.textContent = "Restart";
		const rate = bandwidth() / Number(qualitySelect.value);
		videoResult.textContent =
			rate >= 1
				? "Playing… this connection downloads video faster than it plays."
				: "Playing… this connection downloads video slower than it plays. Watch what happens.";
		last = performance.now();
		videoFrame = requestAnimationFrame(videoTick);
	});

	root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-bl-preset]").forEach((btn) => {
		btn.addEventListener("click", () => {
			bwInput.value = String(BW_STEPS.indexOf(Number(btn.dataset.bw)));
			latInput.value = String(LAT_STEPS.indexOf(Number(btn.dataset.lat)));
			renderSliders();
		});
	});
	bwInput.addEventListener("input", renderSliders);
	latInput.addEventListener("input", renderSliders);

	renderSliders();
	renderVideo();
</script>

<style is:global>
	.bl-demo .bl-presets {
		margin-top: 0;
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-presets .demo-btn {
		font-size: 0.82em;
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-sliders {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 17em), 1fr));
		gap: 0.6em 1.5em;
		margin: 1em auto 0;
		max-width: 44em;
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-slider {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.2em 0.8em;
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-slider label {
		grid-column: 1 / -1;
		font-weight: 600;
		font-size: 0.95em;
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-slider .demo-range {
		width: 100%;
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-slider-value {
		min-width: 5.5em;
		text-align: right;
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-weight: 700;
		font-size: 1.15em;
		color: #fff3d6;
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-panels {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 17em), 1fr));
		gap: 0.8em;
		margin-top: 1em;
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-panel {
		padding: 0.85em 1em;
		border-radius: 12px;
		border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
		background: var(--color-bg);
		text-align: center;
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-panel-title {
		margin: 0 0 0.7em;
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--color-text);
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-panel-result {
		margin: 0.7em 0 0;
		min-height: 3em;
		font-size: 0.92em;
		line-height: 1.45;
		color: var(--color-text);
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-ping-track {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.6em;
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-ping-end {
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-weight: 700;
		font-size: 0.85em;
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-ping-line {
		position: relative;
		flex: 1;
		height: 0.35em;
		border-radius: 999px;
		background: var(--color-border);
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-ping-dot {
		position: absolute;
		top: 50%;
		left: 0;
		width: 1.1em;
		height: 1.1em;
		margin: -0.55em 0 0 -0.55em;
		border-radius: 50%;
		background: var(--color-accent);
		box-shadow: 0 0 10px var(--color-accent);
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-ping-dot.is-returning {
		background: #fff3d6;
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-quality {
		margin-top: 0;
		margin-bottom: 0.6em;
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-video-screen {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		height: 5em;
		border-radius: 8px 8px 0 0;
		background: #000;
		border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
		border-bottom: none;
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-video-screen.is-playing {
		background:
			radial-gradient(circle at 30% 40%, rgba(255, 174, 46, 0.35), transparent 50%),
			radial-gradient(circle at 70% 70%, rgba(255, 243, 214, 0.2), transparent 55%),
			#000;
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-video-bar {
		position: relative;
		height: 0.7em;
		border-radius: 0 0 6px 6px;
		background: var(--color-border);
		overflow: hidden;
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-video-buffered,
	.bl-demo .bl-video-played {
		position: absolute;
		top: 0;
		bottom: 0;
		left: 0;
		width: 0;
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-video-buffered {
		background: #7c8196;
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-video-played {
		background: var(--color-accent);
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-tasks-title {
		margin: 1.2em 0 0.5em;
		text-align: center;
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--color-text);
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-tasks {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.7em;
		margin: 0 auto;
		max-width: 46em;
		padding: 0;
		list-style: none;
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-task {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(9em, 13em) 1fr minmax(6em, auto);
		grid-template-areas:
			"name bar time"
			". note note";
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.2em 0.8em;
		text-align: left;
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-task-name {
		grid-area: name;
		font-size: 0.92em;
		color: var(--color-text);
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-task-bar {
		grid-area: bar;
		display: flex;
		height: 1em;
		border-radius: 4px;
		overflow: hidden;
		background: var(--color-border);
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-task-wait,
	.bl-demo .bl-key--wait {
		background: repeating-linear-gradient(135deg, #7c8196 0 4px, #4a4f63 4px 8px);
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-task-load,
	.bl-demo .bl-key--load {
		background: var(--color-accent);
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-task-time {
		grid-area: time;
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-weight: 700;
		font-size: 0.95em;
		color: #fff3d6;
		white-space: nowrap;
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-task-note {
		grid-area: note;
		font-size: 0.82em;
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-legend {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		justify-content: center;
		gap: 0.4em 1.2em;
		margin-top: 0.8em;
		font-size: 0.85em;
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-legend > span {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.4em;
	}

	.bl-demo .bl-key {
		display: inline-block;
		width: 1.4em;
		height: 0.8em;
		border-radius: 3px;
	}

	@media (max-width: 520px) {
		.bl-demo .bl-task {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
			grid-template-areas:
				"name time"
				"bar bar"
				"note note";
		}
	}
</style>
